   "description": "EL219 is specifically being developed for early antifungal therapy (EAT), when infection is suspected due to highly suggestive signs and symptoms of disease; in high-risk people, antifungals are recommended even before confirmation of the microbial cause of infection, because delayed therapy is associated with poor outcomes in those who lack adequate immune responses. EL219 may provide a once-weekly alternative to LAmB and other polyenes that could also reduce the toxicities that often limit the frequency and duration of administration for these highly efficacious antifungals.",
