   "description": "The Mean change in the Menopause-Specific Quality of Life Questionnaire (MENQOL) measures the impact of menopause symptoms over the last week.\n\nThe questionnaire has 29 items across four domains: vasomotor (items 1 to 3), psychosocial (items 4 to 10), physical (items 11 to 26), and sexual (items 27 to 29). Items pertaining to a specific symptom are rated as present or not present, and if present, how bothersome on a 0 (not bothersome) to 6 (extremely bothersome) scale.\n\nThe mean change in the MENQOL domain scores will be assessed from Baseline to each week measured. A negative change in the score from Baseline to each week measured indicates an improvement in quality of life.",
