   "measure": "Percentage of participants achieving an improved (reduced) weekly average Worst Itch Scale (WIS) score of ≥ 4 from Baseline for participants equal or greater than 6 years old with a weekly average WIS of ≥ 4 at Baseline",
   "description": "The WIS is an assessment tool that participants use to report the intensity of their pruritus. Using an 11-point scale (0 to 10) where 0 indicates no itching and 10 indicates worst itching possible, participants are asked 2 questions: \"What was the worst itch you had today?\" and \"What was the worst itch you had last night?\" The WIS will be administered to participants ≥ 6 years of age at the time of the Baseline visit.",
